  "raw_label": "-1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Vishal S/O. Vijaykumar Baldava vs The State Of Maharashtra And Others on 23 November, 2020 Bench: T.V. Nalawade, Shrikant D. Kulkarni 1 Cri.W.P. No. 445/2020 In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay, Bench At Aurangabad 67. Criminal Writ Petition No.445 Of 2020 Vishal S/o Vijaykumar Baldava, age 30 years occupation business R/o Marwad Galli, Shevgaon Taluka Shevgaon Dist. Ahmednagar ... Petitioner Versus 1. The State of Maharashtra Through its Home Ministry, Mantralaya,Mumbai. 2. The Police Commissioner, Nashik Division, Nashik. 3. The Superintendent of Police, Ahmednagar. 4. The Sub-Divisional Police Officer, Shevgaon Dist. Ahmednagar 5. The Police Inspector, Shevgaon Police Station, Shevgaon Dist. Ahmednagar 6. Shyamsundar S/o Harikishan Dhoot, age 61 years occupation business R/o Marwad Galli, Shevgaon Taluka Shevgaon Dist. Ahmednagar ...Respondents Mr. Shaikh Mazhar A. Jahagirdar, Advocate for petitioner Mr. S.J. Salgare, Addl. Public Prosecutor for Respts. No.1 to 5 Mr. A.D. Ostwal, Advocate for respondent No.6 Coram : T.V. Nalawade & Shrikant D. Kulkarni, Jj. Date : 23rd November, 2020 Order :",
    "facts": "Today the learned Addl. Public Prosecutor produced on record the report of the Police Inspector, Shevgaon Police Station, dated 23rd November 2020. The report shows that the charge-sheet is filed against three persons, like, Shyamsundar Dhoot, Devilal Bihani and Sandip Chintaman. The grievance of the petitioner against Revenue Officers, Officers of the Supply Department, can be considered even by the Trial Court if there is material to show that they had hands in gloves with aforesaid three persons. Learned Counsel Shri Shaikh Mazhar Jahagirdar for the petitioner wants time to go through the charge-sheet and the report. The present proceeding is filed for transfer of investigation of Crime Regn. No. 512 of 2020, which was registered for offences punishable under sections 3 & 7 of the Essential Commodities Act, 1955 and section 419, etc. of the Indian Penal Code. The charge-sheet is filed for these offences and offences punishable under the Indian Penal Code also, like, 419, 468, 471, 34 of I.P.C It is also filed U/s. 33 of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006.",
    "arguments": "",
